      }
    },
    {
      "id": "contract-exposure-and-auth",
      "kind": "invariant",
      "statement": "A contract states its exposure (public, internal or local) and its auth as {scheme, ...} with scheme anonymous, session, service, provisioning-token, signature, signed-address, delegation or in-process; with system.generation set a missing or prose auth is contract.auth-structured and a missing exposure contract.exposure, and always an object auth has only the members of its scheme (contract.auth-structured) and in-process is exactly the scheme of local contracts (contract.exposure); a local contract has no HTTP binding and an internal one none under the gateway prefix (exposure.gateway); a public contract not marked readOnly needs a session or visitor with csrf and origin or a verified credential (auth.public-write); an anonymous public contract is readOnly or justified and limited by a quota, an anonymous internal one readOnly and justified (auth.anonymous); the service scheme is never public (auth.service-public); every named policy governs the contract (auth.policy-unknown); a development contract names a declared condition, is never anonymous and when public names roles (auth.dev-only); and a public contract states a tenantScope other than platform (contract.tenant-scope).",
      "rationale": "Evidence is the core tests of WG-4908 (tests/core/access.test.js): a specification covering every exposure validates clean, prose is accepted only without the switch, and each rule is reported once at its position by a fixture that breaks only it. Supported, not verified, because Exegra does not check its own validation rules.",
      "subjects": [
